50609s1996    nju      bd   000 0 eng    a   95030610  aDLCcDLCdUKMdTNT  aGB96-77269  a35829880  a0691001685 (alk. paper)00aPN1021b.N392 1996  aTNTA14aThe Princeton handbook of multicultural poetries /cT.V.F. Brogan, editor.  aPrinceton, N.J. :bPrinceton University Press,c1996.  axx, 366 p. ;c24 cm.  aArticles are taken from the parent volume, New Princeton encyclopedia of poetry and poetics.  aIncludes bibliographical references. 0aPoetryxDictionaries. 0aPoeticsxDictionaries. 0aPoetryxHistory and criticism.1 aBrogan, T. V. F.q(Terry V. F.)  aPN1021 .N392 1996wLCc1i50706010070978d3/1/2023e1/23/2023f5/20/2025g12lSTACKSmERCn2p$17.95rYsYtBOOKu11/20/1997xBOOK03941cam a2200649   u581107SIRSI20210319034439.6190531s2019    nyuabf   b    001 0beng    a  2019022817  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCOdBDXdORXdOCLCFdYDXdOCLdXYZdIEBdTCHdHBPdCLEdIK2dJAOdOCLCQdDLCdTXMdVP@dILCdOCLCAdNDSdDMOPLdTXKILdGL4dOCLdPX9dT3QdOCLCQdOCLdOCLCQdOCLdOEGdOCLdGYGdTXSVPdOCLCO  a9780525540533q(hardcover)  a0525540539q(hardcover)  z9780525540564q(epub)  a(OCoLC)110421515800aF390.H84bK55 2019  aHIS036040aHIS036130aBIO0060002bisacsh  aMAIN1 aKilmeade, Brian,eauthor4aut10aSam Houston and the Alamo avengers :bthe Texas victory that changed American history /cBrian Kilmeade.30aTexas victory that changed American history14aSam Houston & the Alamo avengers 1a[New York] :bSentinel,c[2019]  a272 pages, 16 unnumbered unnumbered leaves of plates :billustrations (some color), maps ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  mGender group:ngdraMen2lcdgt  mNationality/regional group:nnataNew Yorkers (New York State)2lcdgt  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.  aMaps on endpapers.00tPrologue: The lessons of battle --tGeneral Jackson's Protégé --tGone to Texas --t"Come and Take It" --tConcepción --tA Slow Siege at the Alamo --tThe Defenders --tTwelve Days of Uncertainty --tThe Massacre --tBring Out the Dead --tHouston Hears the News --tFort Defiance --tThe Texian Exodus --tAn Army Assembles --tThe Battle at San Jacinto --t"Remember the Alamo!" --tOld Sam Jacinto --tPresident Sam Houston --tEpilogue: The Founding and the Founders of Texas.  aMarch 1836: The story of the Alamo is familiar to most: more than two hundred Texians trapped in an adobe mission, and massacred. Though the rallying cry of "Remember the Alamo" rang across the country, Houston knew it was poor strategy to aggressively retaliate immediately. One month after the massacre, he and his army of underdog Texians soundly defeated Santa Anna's troops in under eighteen minutes at the Battle of San Jacinto, and in doing so won the independence for which so many had died. Kilmeade brings one of the most pivotal moments in American history to life. -- adapted from jacket  aIngrambShelf ready books10aHouston, Sam,d1793-1863.10aSanta Anna, Antonio López de,d1794-1876. 0aTexasxHistoryyRevolution, 1835-1836. 0aSan Jacinto, Battle of, Tex., 1836. 0aAlamo (San Antonio, Tex.)xSiege, 1836. 0aGovernorszTexasvBiography. 0aLegislatorszUnited StatesvBiography. 0aTexasxHistoryyTo 1846. 1aTexas 1aTexaszSan Antonio. 1aTexasxHistory. 7aHISTORYzUnited Statesx19th Century. 7aUnited StatesxHistoryxState & LocalxSouthwest (AZ, NM, OK, TX) 7aLegislators. 7aAlamo (San Antonio, Tex.), Battle of the, 1836. 7aBattle of San Jacintoc(Texas :d1836)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01404392 7aRevolutionc(Texas :d1835-1836)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01354582 7aSiege of Alamoc(San Antonio, Texas :d1836)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01910462 7aTo 18462fast 7aBiographies.08iOnline version:aKilmeade, Brian.tSam Houston and the Alamo avengers.dNew York : Sentinel, 2019z9780525540564w(DLC)  2019022818  a92bTNT  aF390 .H84 K55 2019wLCc1i50706010953454f6/2/2025g2lSTACKSmERCp$